<lesson id="les-l9-02-n-minus-one" title="One cable may always die" level="9" minutes="20" goal="No ring cable carries more than 70 percent and any single cut still reaches the exchange"/>
<step n="1" text="Two cities push 500 Mbit/s each toward IXMakassar. Open the flow view and read every cable's load: both flows ride the western arc of the ring."/>
<step n="2" text="The cable between PopMakassar and PopParepare carries both flows at once. That is 1000 Mbit/s on a 1000 Mbit/s cable: the day one city holds a football final, the ring chokes."/>
<step n="3" text="Turn on flow spreading, so every flow splits over both arcs of the ring and no cable runs hot." check="c1"/>
<step n="4" text="Hot is not the only danger. If the loaded western cable breaks, PopParepare must still reach the exchange the long way around." check="c2"/>
<step n="5" text="And PopPalu must survive losing its eastern cable too." check="c3"/>
<check id="c1" kind="load" from="pop1" to="links" url="" expect="70" label="No cable is above 70 percent"/>
<check id="c2" kind="outage" from="pop2" to="ix0" url="pop1:GigabitEthernet0/0" expect="ok" label="PopParepare still reaches IXMakassar with the western cable cut"/>
<check id="c3" kind="outage" from="pop3" to="ix0" url="pop3:GigabitEthernet0/1" expect="ok" label="PopPalu still reaches IXMakassar with its eastern cable cut"/>
